@facet-ignore-file
-- docs/facets/schema/assumption.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/assumption.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET Assumption Record",
  "description": "Schema for a FACET assumption record (FACET specification, Appendix A.3).",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "id",
    "statement",
    "review_by",
    "criticality",
    "risk_if_false"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "const": "0.1",
      "description": "FACET schema version. Must be '0.1'."
    },
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^assumption/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
      "description": "Canonical assumption ID in the form assumption/<domain>/<name> (lowercase kebab-case)."
    },
    "statement": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 20,
      "description": "The assumption being made. Written as a positive declarative statement (e.g. 'The host operating system provides a hardware-backed secure enclave accessible via the platform keychain API.')."
    },
    "evidence": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/definitions/evidence_item"
      },
      "description": "Evidence supporting this assumption. An empty array means the assumption is unvalidated.",
      "default": []
    },
    "review_by": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "ISO 8601 date by which this assumption must be reviewed. If the date has passed the assumption is stale."
    },
    "criticality": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "low",
        "medium",
        "high",
        "critical"
      ],
      "description": "How severely incorrect assumptions would impact the system. 'critical' means the feature cannot function safely if false."
    },
    "risk_if_false": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Description of the consequences if this assumption turns out to be incorrect."
    },
    "referenced_by": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "description": "Feature IDs (domain/capability/feature) or policy IDs (policy/<domain>/<name>) that rely on this assumption.",
      "default": []
    }
  },
  "definitions": {
    "evidence_item": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "type",
        "reference",
        "date"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Category of evidence (e.g. 'vendor-sla', 'benchmark', 'audit-report', 'design-doc', 'test-result')."
        },
        "reference": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "URL, file path, or document title that constitutes the evidence."
        },
        "date": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "ISO 8601 date when this evidence was collected or published."
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/data-entity.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/data-entity.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET Data Entity Record",
  "description": "Schema for a FACET data-entity record (FACET specification, Appendix A.4).",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "id",
    "retention",
    "ownership"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "const": "0.1",
      "description": "FACET schema version. Must be '0.1'."
    },
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^data/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
      "description": "Canonical data-entity ID in the form data/<domain>/<entity> (lowercase kebab-case)."
    },
    "canonical_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "fields": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/field"
          },
          "description": "Ordered list of fields in this data entity."
        },
        "version": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Schema version string (e.g. 'v1', '2.0.0', '2024-01-15'). Used to track schema evolution."
        }
      }
    },
    "retention": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "policy"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "policy": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Human-readable description of the retention policy for this entity (e.g. 'Delete on account erasure request', 'Retain for 7 years per financial regulations')."
        },
        "duration": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Maximum retention duration expressed as an ISO 8601 duration or human-readable string (e.g. 'P7Y', '90d', 'indefinite')."
        }
      }
    },
    "ownership": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "team"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "team": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Team that owns this data entity and is responsible for its schema, migrations, and retention enforcement."
        }
      }
    },
    "read_by": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "description": "Feature IDs (domain/capability/feature) or team names that read this entity.",
      "default": []
    },
    "mutated_by": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "description": "Feature IDs (domain/capability/feature) or team names that create, update, or delete records of this entity.",
      "default": []
    }
  },
  "definitions": {
    "field": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "name",
        "type"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Field name as it appears in the canonical data model."
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Data type (e.g. 'string', 'uuid', 'bytes', 'timestamp', 'int64', 'bool', 'object')."
        },
        "constraints": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Validation or database constraints applied to this field (e.g. 'not-null', 'unique', 'max-length:255', 'encrypted-at-rest').",
          "default": []
        },
        "references": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "If this field is a foreign key or logical reference, the data-entity ID it points to (e.g. 'data/crm/customer-account')."
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/facet.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/facet.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET Feature Record",
  "description": "Schema for a FACET feature record (FACET specification, Appendix A.1).",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "id",
    "intent",
    "contract",
    "lineage"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "0.1"
      ],
      "description": "FACET record schema version. A record declaring variants cannot also declare a top-level lifecycle."
    },
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
      "description": "Canonical feature ID in the form domain/capability/feature (3 lowercase kebab-case segments)."
    },
    "lifecycle": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "planned",
        "active",
        "deprecated",
        "sunset"
      ],
      "description": "Current lifecycle state of the feature. 'planned' = documented but not yet implemented (no source anchor required); 'active' = implemented and deployed (source anchor enforced by CI); 'deprecated' = being phased out; 'sunset' = removed."
    },
    "intent": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "summary"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "summary": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 20,
          "maxLength": 1500,
          "description": "Human-readable description of what the feature does and why it exists."
        },
        "decision_records": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "References to ADR or other decision records that motivated this feature.",
          "default": []
        }
      }
    },
    "contract": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "scenarios"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "scenarios": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/scenario"
          },
          "description": "Behavioral contract expressed as Gherkin-style scenarios."
        },
        "business_rules": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/business_rule"
          },
          "description": "Business rules and formulas this feature applies, each kept in a DMN model and referenced here, never copied (FACET §3.2.4). The model is the source of the rule's logic; this entry names it, says in one line what it fixes, and links it to the scenarios that are cases of it. The core reads only these fields and never opens the model."
        }
      }
    },
    "verification": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "unit_tests": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/test_ref"
          },
          "description": "Unit test references mapped to contract scenario IDs."
        },
        "property_tests": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/test_ref"
          },
          "description": "Property-based test references mapped to contract scenario IDs."
        },
        "integration_tests": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/test_ref"
          },
          "description": "Integration test references mapped to contract scenario IDs."
        },
        "e2e_tests": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/test_ref"
          },
          "description": "End-to-end test references mapped to contract scenario IDs."
        }
      }
    },
    "observation": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "slos": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/slo"
          },
          "description": "Service level objectives for this feature."
        },
        "alerts": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/alert"
          },
          "description": "Alert definitions that fire when the feature degrades."
        },
        "dashboards": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "url"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "url": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "URL to a Grafana or other dashboard for this feature."
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Links to observability dashboards."
        },
        "continuous_checks": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/continuous_check"
          },
          "description": "Synthetic checks run continuously against this feature."
        }
      }
    },
    "observability": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Developer-facing emission contract: metric names, span names and log events actually emitted by the implementation. Peer of operator-facing 'observation', which defines SLOs, alerts and runbooks for judging health. Emitted names allow alert conditions to be compared with the implementation. Every list is optional; an absent block claims nothing about emissions.",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "metrics_emitted": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/metric_emission"
          },
          "description": "Metrics this feature emits."
        },
        "traces_emitted": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/trace_emission"
          },
          "description": "Trace spans this feature emits."
        },
        "log_events": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/log_event"
          },
          "description": "Structured log events this feature emits."
        }
      }
    },
    "defects": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Fixes landed in this feature's anchored code, one entry per bugfix commit with its date and touched files. Counts are derived from the fixes list; per-file counts are derived from paths in that list.",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "fixes": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/defect_fix"
          },
          "description": "One entry per bugfix commit attributed to this feature. Append-only in practice: a tool adds entries it has not seen before and never rewrites one, so a hand-corrected entry survives the next run."
        },
        "excluded": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/defect_exclusion"
          },
          "description": "Commits excluded from this feature’s defect ledger, with the reason. Backfill preserves these exclusions."
        }
      }
    },
    "knowledge": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "User-facing knowledge facet. Captures the questions a user-facing knowledge base must answer for this feature, plus the non-derivable facts only the feature owner can supply. Optional: empty or absent knowledge produces a linter warning, never an error. Slots are authored as questions (or short answers to invariant questions); the LLM-driven generator pipeline (see FACET §8.5) renders user-facing artifacts (FAQ, help-center articles) by combining these slots with the feature's intent, contract, and source anchors.",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "prerequisite_knowledge": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/knowledge_slot",
          "description": "What the user must already understand to use this feature successfully (e.g. 'understands what a webhook is', 'has admin permissions on Billing'). Not derivable from source."
        },
        "not_for": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/knowledge_slot",
          "description": "Anti-use-cases: situations where this feature is the wrong tool. Owner-supplied; an LLM cannot infer absence-of-fit from source."
        },
        "discoverability": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/knowledge_slot",
          "description": "Where and how the user enters or finds this feature in the product (UI path, CLI command, API endpoint, deep link). The answer may be derivable from source/anchors; the question is invariant."
        },
        "common_pitfalls": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/knowledge_slot",
          "description": "Frequent mistakes users make with this feature, and how to recognize/avoid them. Drawn from support tickets, owner experience, or contract failure scenarios."
        },
        "success_signal": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/knowledge_slot",
          "description": "How the user knows the feature worked for them — the felt confirmation, not the system post-state. Owner-supplied."
        }
      }
    },
    "lineage": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "owner",
        "created_at"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "specified_by": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*:([0-9]{3}-|[0-9]+-[0-9]+-)?[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(/([0-9]{3}-|[0-9]+-[0-9]+-)?[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)*$"
          },
          "uniqueItems": true
        },
        "owner": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/owner"
        },
        "created_at": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "ISO 8601 date when this record was first created (YYYY-MM-DD)."
        },
        "superseded_by": {
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Feature ID that replaces this one, or null if not superseded."
        },
        "depends_on": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Feature IDs that this feature depends on.",
          "default": []
        },
        "depended_on_by": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Feature IDs that depend on this feature.",
          "default": []
        },
        "related_policies": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Policy IDs (policy/<domain>/<name>) that govern this feature.",
          "default": []
        },
        "related_assumptions": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Assumption IDs (assumption/<domain>/<name>) that this feature relies on.",
          "default": []
        },
        "related_data_entities": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Data entity IDs (data/<domain>/<entity>) that this feature reads or mutates.",
          "default": []
        },
        "change_history_ref": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Pointer to a CHANGELOG section or git tag range for this feature's history."
        },
        "tickets": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/ticket_ref"
          },
          "uniqueItems": true,
          "default": [],
          "description": "Issues in a tracker that are relevant to this feature as a whole. Optional, and independent of the scenarios' 'tickets': the framework does not say where a given ticket belongs (FACET §3.7.1). See definitions/ticket_ref."
        }
      }
    },
    "authorship": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Per-section authorship metadata (free-form). Typically injected by the FACET agent.",
      "additionalProperties": true
    },
    "metadata": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Tool-generated provenance and annotation map. Keys and values are strings capped at 1000 characters. Authorship is recorded separately.",
      "propertyNames": {
        "maxLength": 1000
      },
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "string",
        "maxLength": 1000
      }
    },
    "variants": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Per-variant lifecycle state, keyed by names declared in variants.yaml. An absent variant does not apply. A record with variants cannot also declare a top-level lifecycle.",
      "minProperties": 1,
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "patternProperties": {
        "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "lifecycle"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "lifecycle": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "planned",
                "active",
                "deprecated",
                "sunset"
              ],
              "description": "Lifecycle of this feature on this variant. 'active' requires an anchor in a path exclusive to it; shared code proves no variant."
            },
            "notes": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Why this variant differs, when that is not obvious."
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "flags": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Feature flags controlling exposure, independently of lifecycle.",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/definitions/feature_flag"
      },
      "default": []
    }
  },
  "definitions": {
    "scenario": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "statement"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
          "description": "Stable kebab-case identifier for this scenario, unique within the feature."
        },
        "specified_by": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*:([0-9]{3}-|[0-9]+-[0-9]+-)?[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(/([0-9]{3}-|[0-9]+-[0-9]+-)?[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)*#[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
        },
        "statement": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Gherkin-style prose statement (Given/When/Then or equivalent natural language)."
        },
        "examples": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "description": "Named example blocks for a parameterised Gherkin Scenario Outline. A <name> placeholder substitutes values from the named column. Blocks without columns inherit the first declared columns; blocks may declare different columns. Each block describes one rule. The linter checks row widths and warns on undeclared placeholders (FACET §11.2). The outline counts as one scenario regardless of its number of cases.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/examples_block"
          },
          "contains": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "columns"
            ]
          }
        },
        "audience": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "product",
            "engineering"
          ],
          "description": "Readership of the scenario statement: product uses product language readable without implementation knowledge; engineering requires implementation knowledge. Absence means unclassified. This classification changes neither lint findings nor scenario counts."
        },
        "pre_state": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Optional structured description of the system state required before this scenario.",
          "additionalProperties": true
        },
        "post_state": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Optional structured description of the observable system state after this scenario.",
          "additionalProperties": true
        },
        "variants": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Variants this scenario applies to. Omit when it applies everywhere the feature exists."
        },
        "backing": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/backing"
        },
        "deviation": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/deviation"
        },
        "tickets": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/ticket_ref"
          },
          "uniqueItems": true,
          "default": [],
          "description": "Issues in a tracker that are relevant to this one promise. Optional, and independent of 'lineage.tickets' (FACET §3.7.1). See definitions/ticket_ref."
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "required": [
              "deviation"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "backing": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "state": {
                    "const": "backed"
                  },
                  "by_variant": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "patternProperties": {
                      "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "state": {
                            "const": "backed"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "examples_block": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "One named set of cases under a Scenario Outline: a heading row and the rows beneath it, for one rule.\n\nThe object accepts the declared 'columns' key and rejects unknown keys, including 'cols'. Explicit columns determine how row values are interpreted; when columns are omitted, headings are inherited from the outline.",
      "required": [
        "rows"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Optional heading describing what the cases in this block have in common."
        },
        "columns": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "description": "Ordered column names substituted by matching <name> placeholders. When omitted, columns are inherited from the first block declaring them. At least one block must declare columns. Unreferenced columns may carry supporting information."
        },
        "rows": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "description": "Cases as arrays of scalar values matched positionally to the columns in effect. Each row must match the column count; the linter enforces this constraint (FACET §11.2).",
          "items": {
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "items": {
              "description": "One scalar cell substituted into statement prose. An empty string represents an empty value; null is not accepted.",
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "number"
                },
                {
                  "type": "boolean"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "deviation": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Observed unintended behaviour in the anchored code, stated in the code’s own terms. The scenario id names the observed behaviour. The reason records evidence for classifying it as unintended; intended replacement behaviour is referenced through tracked_as. A deviation cannot accompany unbacked backing, including per-variant overrides.",
      "required": [
        "reason"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Code evidence supporting the claim that the observed behaviour is unintended."
        },
        "confirmed_by": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "code-review",
            "test",
            "runtime"
          ],
          "description": "Evidence used to confirm the behaviour: code review, reproduction, or production observation."
        },
        "tracked_as": {
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Issue reference or canonical feature id tracking replacement behaviour. A feature id is resolved and warns if its record becomes active while the deviation remains declared. Other strings are not resolved. Explicit null means nothing tracks this deviation."
        }
      }
    },
    "backing": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Whether the data described by this scenario exists. An absent block means backed. Unbacked means the surface ships with an intended empty state. Per-variant overrides replace the shared state for that variant alone. Record-level backing is derived from scenarios.",
      "required": [
        "state"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "state": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/backing_state"
        },
        "reason": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/backing_reason"
        },
        "unblocked_by": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/backing_unblocked_by"
        },
        "by_variant": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Per-variant overrides of the shared scenario backing state. An absent override uses the shared state.",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "patternProperties": {
            "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$": {
              "$ref": "#/definitions/backing_override"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "state": {
                "const": "unbacked"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "state"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "required": [
              "reason",
              "unblocked_by"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "backing_override": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Override of shared backing for one variant. An unbacked override requires its own reason and unblocked_by reference.",
      "required": [
        "state"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "state": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/backing_state"
        },
        "reason": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/backing_reason"
        },
        "unblocked_by": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/backing_unblocked_by"
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "state": {
                "const": "unbacked"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "state"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "required": [
              "reason",
              "unblocked_by"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "backing_state": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "backed",
        "unbacked"
      ],
      "description": "'backed' — the data this scenario reads exists. 'unbacked' — it deliberately does not yet, and the surface shows whatever it shows without it."
    },
    "backing_reason": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "Why the data is not available yet. Required when state is 'unbacked' to distinguish a declared gap from an unexplained omission."
    },
    "backing_unblocked_by": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "What would supply the data — a store, a domain, a service, or an issue reference. Required when state is 'unbacked'. Written as a feature id in the canonical domain/capability/feature form it becomes an edge in the dependency graph rather than a note, and the linter can then say when the named feature went active and the gap was never revisited."
    },
    "defect_fix": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "One bugfix commit and the anchored files in it that resolve to this feature. The commit and paths provide traceable evidence for an attribution derived by a heuristic; they are not an independently stored counter.",
      "required": [
        "commit",
        "date",
        "files"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "commit": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{7,40}$",
          "description": "Commit hash, lowercase hex. Written in full by tooling so it stays unambiguous as the history grows; a hand-written abbreviation of seven characters or more is accepted and matched by prefix."
        },
        "date": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$",
          "description": "ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD) the commit was authored, retaining recency without resolving the commit in a clone."
        },
        "files": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "description": "Repository-relative paths changed by the commit that carry an anchor for this feature. These paths are the evidence for per-file and per-feature attribution."
        },
        "subject": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The commit's subject line, so the record says what broke without a clone to hand."
        },
        "issue": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Issue or ticket reference the fix names, when it names one."
        },
        "recorded_by": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "git-history",
            "tracker",
            "manual"
          ],
          "description": "Origin of the attribution: Git history, a tracker, or a manual entry. This distinguishes heuristic attribution from human reporting."
        }
      }
    },
    "defect_exclusion": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Commit excluded from this feature’s defect ledger, with a reviewable reason.",
      "required": [
        "commit",
        "reason"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "commit": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{7,40}$",
          "description": "Commit hash, lowercase hex, matched by prefix against the candidates a backfill finds."
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Why this commit is not a defect in this feature — it touched the anchored file only to reformat it, it fixed a neighbouring feature the same commit happened to include, the message says 'fix' about something that was never broken."
        }
      }
    },
    "metric_emission": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "name",
        "kind"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Metric name as emitted to the metrics backend (e.g. 'orders_checkout_requests_total')."
        },
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "counter",
            "gauge",
            "histogram",
            "summary"
          ],
          "description": "OpenMetrics-style metric kind."
        },
        "labels": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Label keys attached to the metric."
        },
        "description": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Free-form description of what the metric measures."
        }
      }
    },
    "trace_emission": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "span_name"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "span_name": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Span name as emitted (e.g. 'orders.checkout')."
        },
        "parent_span": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Expected parent span name when this feature is invoked via the usual call path."
        },
        "attributes": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Span attribute keys attached to this span."
        }
      }
    },
    "log_event": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "event",
        "level"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "event": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Stable log event name / msg field value."
        },
        "level": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "debug",
            "info",
            "warn",
            "error",
            "fatal"
          ],
          "description": "Log level at which the event is emitted."
        },
        "attributes": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Structured-log field keys attached to this event."
        }
      }
    },
    "test_ref": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "proves"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Stable identifier for this test (file path, test name, or CI job ID)."
        },
        "proves": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "description": "List of scenario IDs from contract.scenarios that this test verifies."
        }
      }
    },
    "slo": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "name",
        "target",
        "window"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Human-readable SLO name."
        },
        "target": {
          "type": "number",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 100,
          "description": "Target percentage (0–100)."
        },
        "window": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Rolling window duration (e.g. '30d', '7d', '1h')."
        },
        "query": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "PromQL or equivalent query expression for this SLO."
        },
        "query_source": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Source system for the query (e.g. 'prometheus', 'grafana', 'datadog')."
        }
      }
    },
    "alert": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "name"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Alert rule name."
        },
        "condition": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "PromQL or natural-language condition that triggers the alert."
        },
        "severity": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Alert severity level (e.g. 'critical', 'warning', 'info')."
        },
        "runbook": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "URL or path to the runbook for responding to this alert."
        }
      }
    },
    "continuous_check": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "frequency"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Stable identifier for this synthetic check."
        },
        "frequency": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "How often the check runs (e.g. '1m', '5m', '15m')."
        }
      }
    },
    "owner": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "team"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "team": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Owning team name."
        },
        "individual": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Optional email of the individual DRI for this feature."
        }
      }
    },
    "knowledge_slot": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "question": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 5,
          "description": "User-facing question answered by this slot, for example: 'Which permissions does the user need to apply a discount code?'"
        },
        "answer": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Optional short answer (or list of bullets in plain text) the owner provides for facts that are not derivable from source. Leave empty if the LLM generator can derive the answer from anchors, dependencies, or tests."
        },
        "not_applicable": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Owner-supplied declaration that this question does not apply to the feature. Agents must not supply it. Silences only this slot. Cannot accompany an answer, a non-empty derive_from, or their per-variant forms.",
          "required": [
            "reason",
            "confirmed_by"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "reason": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "Reviewable explanation of why the question does not apply to this feature’s users."
            },
            "confirmed_by": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "Person or owning team declaring that this question does not apply. Required; recorded as text and not resolved against the registry."
            }
          }
        },
        "derive_from": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "anchors",
              "tests",
              "dependencies",
              "policies",
              "data_entities",
              "intent",
              "contract"
            ]
          },
          "description": "Additional record sections or repository sources loaded by the knowledge generator when rendering this slot.",
          "default": []
        },
        "by_variant": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Per-variant overrides. The slot's own answer is the shared default; an override replaces it for that client only. An absent override is not a gap — it means the shared answer applies.",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "patternProperties": {
            "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "answer": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "derive_from": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "anchors",
                      "tests",
                      "dependencies",
                      "policies",
                      "data_entities",
                      "intent",
                      "contract"
                    ]
                  },
                  "description": "Additional record sections or repository sources loaded by the knowledge generator when rendering this slot.",
                  "default": []
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "required": [
              "not_applicable"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "answer": {
                "maxLength": 0
              },
              "derive_from": {
                "maxItems": 0
              },
              "by_variant": {
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "patternProperties": {
                  "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$": {
                    "properties": {
                      "answer": {
                        "maxLength": 0
                      },
                      "derive_from": {
                        "maxItems": 0
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "feature_flag": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "key"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "key": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "The flag key as it appears in source. The linter checks it still does: a declared key that no longer appears anywhere means the gate was removed and the record was not told."
        },
        "system": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Flag system, e.g. launchdarkly, statsig, unleash, env, custom."
        },
        "default": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "Default value when the flag system is unreachable."
        },
        "variants": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Variants this flag gates, when a rollout differs per variant. Omit when it gates every variant."
        },
        "rollout": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Who currently sees it, in plain words."
        },
        "retire_by": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD) by which the flag should be removed. After this date the linter warns but does not fail."
        }
      }
    },
    "business_rule": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "kind",
        "model",
        "element",
        "states"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One business rule: a decision table or a formula in a DMN model.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
          "description": "Stable kebab-case name, unique among this feature's business rules. Not the DMN element id: that belongs to the modeler and changes when a node is renamed there."
        },
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "table",
            "formula"
          ],
          "description": "'table' for a decision table, 'formula' for a literal expression (also inside a business knowledge model). Decides what can be checked and how the rule is shown."
        },
        "model": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "pattern": "^[^/].*\\.dmn$",
          "description": "Path of the DMN model from the repository root, ending in .dmn."
        },
        "element": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Id of the decision or business knowledge model inside 'model'."
        },
        "states": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "One line saying what the rule fixes, for a reader who does not open the model. Not a second description of the logic — that is the model's."
        },
        "scenarios": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
          },
          "uniqueItems": true,
          "description": "Ids of this feature's contract scenarios that are cases of this rule. Says that a scenario is a case; which row it hits is computed by whoever evaluates the model. Absent or empty means no scenario is known to be a case of the rule."
        },
        "completeness": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "claimed",
            "not-claimed"
          ],
          "description": "Only for kind 'table': whether the author claims the table answers every input combination. A claim, not a proof — whatever evaluates the model checks it where it can and says where it cannot."
        }
      },
      "if": {
        "properties": {
          "kind": {
            "const": "formula"
          }
        }
      },
      "then": {
        "not": {
          "required": [
            "completeness"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "ticket_ref": {
      "description": "Issue reference in a tracker and its relation to this feature. A bare key (KAN-12 or example-org/project#123) means relates. The object form specifies a key, relation, optional tracker and title. References do not change lifecycle, backing, or verification.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "maxLength": 200,
          "description": "The issue key as the tracker writes it, relation 'relates'."
        },
        {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "key"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "key": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "maxLength": 200,
              "description": "The issue key as the tracker writes it: 'KAN-12' for Jira, 'owner/repo#481' for GitHub."
            },
            "relation": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "implements",
                "specifies",
                "verifies",
                "tracks-defect",
                "relates"
              ],
              "default": "relates",
              "description": "How the issue relates to this feature. 'implements': the issue asked for this behaviour to be built or changed. 'specifies': the issue is where the behaviour was decided — an epic, a spec ticket, a design review. 'verifies': the issue tracks testing or acceptance of the behaviour. 'tracks-defect': the issue tracks a defect in the behaviour — prefer 'deviation.tracked_as' on the scenario when the defect is declared there. 'relates': anything else. A closed list, so a host can group and filter by it; a relation that fits none is 'relates', not a new word."
            },
            "tracker": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
              "maxLength": 60,
              "description": "Which tracker the key belongs to, by the id under 'trackers' in .facetrc.yaml. Absent means the project's default tracker. Needed only in a project that keeps issues in more than one place."
            },
            "title": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 200,
              "description": "The issue's title as a reader's aid. Not kept in sync with the tracker; a host that can read the tracker shows the live title instead."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "required": [
        "lifecycle"
      ],
      "not": {
        "required": [
          "variants"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "required": [
        "variants"
      ],
      "not": {
        "required": [
          "lifecycle"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
-- docs/facets/schema/facetrc.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/facetrc.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET project configuration",
  "description": "Committed project layout for FACET, read from .facetrc.yaml at the repository root. Optional: a project that omits the file keeps the defaults. Declare either the single-registry fields or a registries block, never both.",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "spec_sources": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "id",
          "repo"
        ],
        "if": {
          "required": [
            "format"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "format": {
              "enum": [
                "speckit",
                "kiro",
                "bmad",
                "gauge"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "then": {
          "not": {
            "required": [
              "runner"
            ]
          }
        },
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
          },
          "repo": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "path": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Defaults to openspec/specs for openspec, specs for speckit and gauge, .kiro/specs for kiro, _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts for bmad, and the repository root for the other formats."
          },
          "follow": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "default": "main"
          },
          "format": {
            "enum": [
              "facet-spec",
              "gherkin",
              "openspec",
              "speckit",
              "gherkin-markdown",
              "kiro",
              "bmad",
              "gauge"
            ],
            "default": "facet-spec"
          },
          "runner": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
            "description": "Declared cucumber-json runner used to execute pinned scenarios."
          },
          "registries": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
            },
            "uniqueItems": true
          }
        }
      },
      "uniqueItems": true
    },
    "test_feature_prefixes": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1
      },
      "description": "Explicit feature ID prefixes for several parts of one tested product."
    },
    "test_feature_prefix": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Explicit feature ID prefix for test discovery claims and execution reports. Empty selects every feature."
    },
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "0.1"
      ],
      "description": "FACET version this configuration is written against."
    },
    "adr": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Project-wide ADR reader configuration.",
      "properties": {
        "directory": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^(([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)(/[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)*)?$",
          "description": "ADR directory relative to the repository root. Omitted or empty uses docs/adr.",
          "default": "docs/adr"
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "bpmn": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Project-wide BPMN reader configuration.",
      "properties": {
        "directory": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^(([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)(/[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)*)?$",
          "description": "BPMN directory relative to repository root.",
          "default": "docs/bpmn"
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "records": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/relativeDir",
      "description": "Where feature records live. Default: docs/facets"
    },
    "schema": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/relativeDir",
      "description": "Where the JSON schemas live. Derived from the records directory when absent."
    },
    "sources": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/sources",
      "description": "Directories scanned for @facet: anchors. Absent means the whole repository, minus whatever .gitignore excludes."
    },
    "registries": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "One entry per independent product in a monorepo. Use this only when the products' feature lists are not comparable — a rewrite, a native app, or any second implementation of the same product is a variant (see variants.yaml), not a registry.",
      "minProperties": 1,
      "propertyNames": {
        "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
        "description": "A registry name prefixes ids in qualified anchors, so it follows the id segment grammar."
      },
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "records": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/relativeDir",
            "description": "Where this registry's records live."
          },
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/relativeDir"
          },
          "sources": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/sources",
            "description": "Directories this registry owns. Two registries may list the same directory: shared code is scanned by both, and an anchor there resolves against whichever of them has the record."
          },
          "description": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What this registry documents, in one line. Shown when the tooling has to name it."
          },
          "runners": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/runners"
          },
          "conventions": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/conventionsPath",
            "description": "This registry's own conventions document. A deliberate override: it replaces the project-level document for this registry, and the two are never merged."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "records"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    "conventions": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/conventionsPath",
      "description": "The project's authoring conventions document (prose language, protected terminology, what a summary is for, where unresolved claims go), shared by every registry that declares none of its own. Absent means FACET-CONVENTIONS.md at the repository root if it exists, and none otherwise. Read by people and agents; never executed or interpreted by tooling, and it cannot grant permissions or replace human acceptance."
    },
    "forges": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Which forge runs behind a git host, for the hosts this tooling cannot recognise. A hostname does not say what is behind it — git.example.com is a GitLab in one company and a Gitea in the next — so a self-hosted GitLab or a GitHub Enterprise is declared rather than guessed. Absent is the ordinary case: github.com and gitlab.com are recognised, and any other host is reported as undeclared rather than as neither.",
      "minProperties": 1,
      "propertyNames": {
        "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9]([A-Za-z0-9.-]*[A-Za-z0-9])?$",
        "description": "The host of the git remote, as it appears between the '@' or the '://' and the path — git.example.com, not https://git.example.com/team/repo.git."
      },
      "additionalProperties": {
        "enum": [
          "github",
          "gitlab"
        ],
        "description": "Supported forges for pull requests: GitHub through gh and GitLab through glab."
      }
    },
    "embedding": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Project-wide retrieval model settings. Remote egress approval and credential selection are invocation-only and must not be stored here.",
      "properties": {
        "provider": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "base_url": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "model": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "dimensions": {
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "batch": {
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "index": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "error_codes": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Configures the identifier pattern 'facet errors' and the error-codes lint check scan for. Applies to the whole project, not to one registry — a numbering convention spans every registry the same way it spans every team.",
      "properties": {
        "pattern": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Regular expression matching one stable identifier. Default when absent: 'E\\d{4}' (for example, E1074). The pattern is a project convention, not a FACET concept — any project with stable identifiers in its scenario text can declare its own."
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "requires": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Versions this project requires of the FACET tooling. Project-level, also in a project with several registries. Every command except version, help, completion, setup and the git filters 'filter clean|smudge' fails before doing any work when the running Core is not the pinned version or the pin is malformed; agent hooks and MCP tool results report it instead.",
      "properties": {
        "core": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^v?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(-((0|[1-9][0-9]*|[0-9]*[a-zA-Z-][0-9a-zA-Z-]*)(\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*|[0-9]*[a-zA-Z-][0-9a-zA-Z-]*))*))?(\\+[0-9a-zA-Z-]+(\\.[0-9a-zA-Z-]+)*)?$",
          "description": "Exact Core product version pin, with an optional leading v. When the pin has no +build metadata, the running binary's build metadata is ignored; a pin containing metadata requires it to match. Prerelease identifiers remain significant. No ranges or prefixes are accepted."
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "hooks": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Project-wide switches for the guards that run around an agent's commits and turns. Absent means every guard is on. Read from the committed file at HEAD, never from the working tree, so turning a guard off is itself a reviewed commit; the environment variable FACET_SKIP_COMMIT_GATE=1 remains the per-session escape hatch and wins over this.",
      "properties": {
        "commit_gate": {
          "enum": [
            "on",
            "off"
          ],
          "description": "'off' stops the plugin's commit gate from judging this project's commits. Default: on."
        },
        "drift_notice": {
          "enum": [
            "on",
            "off"
          ],
          "description": "'off' stops the Stop hook from reporting drift at the end of a turn. The environment variable FACET_SKIP_DRIFT_NOTICE=1 does the same for one session and wins over this. Default: on."
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "runners": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/runners"
    },
    "trackers": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Where this project keeps its issues, and how a ticket key a record names (FACET §3.7.1) maps to one of them. A record's tickets carry what a specification does not: why something was built, why now, by whom. This list lets a reader — an agent above all — tell which tracker a key belongs to and open it.\n\nResolution, in order: the tracker a reference names with 'tracker'; else the first entry whose 'pattern' matches the key; else the entry marked 'default'. A key nothing resolves stays a bare key, never an invented link.\n\nNo credentials, ever. A private tracker is reached with the caller's own access — an MCP connector, a token in the agent's environment — and this file only says where it is.",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "id"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "if": {
          "required": [
            "format"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "format": {
              "const": "speckit"
            }
          }
        },
        "then": {
          "not": {
            "required": [
              "runner"
            ]
          }
        },
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
            "maxLength": 60,
            "description": "The name a ticket reference uses in its 'tracker' field. A slug, like a taxonomy segment."
          },
          "pattern": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "description": "A regular expression (RE2 syntax) a key of this tracker matches, anchored by the author: '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+-[0-9]+$' for Jira, '^(?P<repo>[^#]+)#(?P<number>[0-9]+)$' for GitHub. Named groups become placeholders in 'url'. A pattern that does not compile is a configuration error."
          },
          "url": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "description": "Link template for one issue. '{key}' is the whole key; every named group of 'pattern' is available by its name. Example: 'https://example.atlassian.net/browse/{key}'."
          },
          "default": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "The tracker a key belongs to when no pattern matches. At most one entry may set it; a key resolved this way is reported as resolved by default."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "source_views": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Opt-in portable repository identities and named coherent source views. Local checkout paths belong only in ignored .facet/sources.local.yaml. Legacy sources remain path filters.",
      "properties": {
        "repositories": {
          "type": "object",
          "minProperties": 1,
          "propertyNames": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
          },
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "description": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          }
        },
        "registry_repository": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
          "description": "Explicit logical identity of the registry repository; does not change the record root or add another source checkout."
        },
        "default_view": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
        },
        "views": {
          "type": "object",
          "minProperties": 1,
          "propertyNames": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
          },
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "sources": {
                "type": "object",
                "minProperties": 1,
                "propertyNames": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
                },
                "additionalProperties": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "binding": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
                    },
                    "ref": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Optional Git ref, which must resolve to the commit checked out by the selected binding."
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "binding"
                  ],
                  "additionalProperties": false
                }
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "sources"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false
          }
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "repositories",
        "views"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  },
  "not": {
    "description": "Top-level records/sources and a registries block are mutually exclusive; use one registry layout to keep registry selection unambiguous.",
    "anyOf": [
      {
        "required": [
          "registries",
          "records"
        ]
      },
      {
        "required": [
          "registries",
          "sources"
        ]
      },
      {
        "required": [
          "registries",
          "schema"
        ]
      },
      {
        "required": [
          "registries",
          "runners"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "additionalProperties": {
    "type": "object",
    "description": "A top-level section this schema does not define belongs to an installed product, which reads and validates it. Core accepts it as long as it is a mapping, so a project that configures a product keeps working with a FACET build that does not carry the product."
  },
  "$defs": {
    "relativeDir": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "pattern": "^[^/].*[^/]$|^[^/]$",
      "description": "Repository-relative directory, without a leading or trailing slash."
    },
    "conventionsPath": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "pattern": "^[^/].*[^/]$|^[^/]$",
      "not": {
        "pattern": "(^|/)\\.\\.(/|$)"
      },
      "description": "Repository-relative file path, without a leading slash and never climbing out of the repository."
    },
    "sources": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "uniqueItems": true,
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/relativeDir"
      }
    },
    "runners": {
      "type": "object",
      "propertyNames": {
        "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
      },
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "command": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": ".*\\S.*"
          },
          "list": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "cwd": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/relativeDir"
          },
          "report": {
            "enum": [
              "junit",
              "go-json",
              "cucumber-json"
            ]
          },
          "report_file": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/relativeDir"
          },
          "list_format": {
            "enum": [
              "lines",
              "json"
            ],
            "description": "Discovery output: newline paths (default), or a JSON array of paths or objects with explicit file fields."
          },
          "repository": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
            "description": "Logical repository selected from source_views for discovery and execution."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "command"
        ],
        "dependentRequired": {
          "report": [
            "report_file"
          ],
          "report_file": [
            "report"
          ],
          "list_format": [
            "list"
          ]
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/generation-manifest.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/generation-manifest.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET Generation Manifest",
  "description": "Committed provenance for generated documentation (FACET §8.6), naming input resources and digests so changes can invalidate an artifact. Resource fields use in-toto ResourceDescriptor vocabulary, so a deployment that later needs signed provenance can map onto SLSA without redesigning the format.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "artifacts"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "0.1"
      ],
      "description": "FACET schema family this manifest was written under."
    },
    "artifacts": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "One entry per generated artifact, sorted by subject path so the diff stays reviewable.",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/definitions/artifact"
      }
    }
  },
  "definitions": {
    "digest": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "sha256"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "sha256": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$",
          "description": "SHA-256 of the file's contents. Content hashing is deliberate: git does not preserve modification times, so a timestamp comparison would mark every artifact stale after a fresh clone."
        }
      }
    },
    "artifact": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "subject",
        "feature",
        "generator",
        "inputs"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "subject": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "path",
            "digest"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "The generated artifact itself.",
          "properties": {
            "path": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Repository-relative path to the generated file."
            },
            "digest": {
              "$ref": "#/definitions/digest"
            }
          }
        },
        "feature": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
          "description": "Feature id the artifact was generated from."
        },
        "slots": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "prerequisite_knowledge",
              "not_for",
              "discoverability",
              "common_pitfalls",
              "success_signal"
            ]
          },
          "description": "Knowledge slots the artifact consumed. Recording these allows per-slot staleness rather than invalidating a whole article when one unrelated slot's sources move.",
          "default": []
        },
        "generator": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "pipeline"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "The non-hermetic part of the build. An LLM is not a deterministic compiler, so the model and prompt version are inputs: changing either invalidates the artifact exactly as a new compiler would.",
          "properties": {
            "pipeline": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Name of the generator pipeline."
            },
            "model": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Model that produced the artifact."
            },
            "prompt_version": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Version of the generation prompt."
            }
          }
        },
        "generated_at": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "ISO 8601 date of generation (YYYY-MM-DD). Narration only — never used as a comparison key."
        },
        "inputs": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "description": "Everything that fed the artifact: the feature record, plus every source file anchoring that feature at generation time. The resolved set is recorded in full, because FACET resolves anchors by scanning source — an anchor added later is a real change even when every recorded digest still matches.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "role",
              "uri",
              "digest"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "role": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "record",
                  "anchor",
                  "source-artifact",
                  "glossary"
                ],
                "description": "Input role: record is the feature record; anchor is implementing source; source-artifact is the source-language article; glossary is consulted terminology. A changed glossary invalidates artifacts that used it."
              },
              "uri": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Repository-relative path to the input."
              },
              "digest": {
                "$ref": "#/definitions/digest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "locale": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "BCP 47 language tag for this artifact. A translation depends on the source-language article and record: a record change invalidates the source article, and its regeneration invalidates the translation. Records remain in their canonical language: two normative statements of one behaviour have no tie-break when they diverge."
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/glossary.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/glossary.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET Project Glossary",
  "description": "Optional naming authority for terms of art used in record prose. It carries definitions, not contracts, anchors or lifecycle. Consumers may link exact, case-sensitive, whole-word occurrences without adding references or markup to records. Without this file, glossary checks do not run.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "terms"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "0.1"
      ],
      "description": "FACET schema family this glossary was written under."
    },
    "categories": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Optional flat category list in display order. Categories have no parents or children. Terms may reference one declared category. Undeclared references and duplicate IDs are errors; unused categories produce warnings. Without categories, terms remain an ungrouped list.",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/definitions/category"
      }
    },
    "terms": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Terms in project-defined order. Each entry carries its own name and definition; names may contain spaces.",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/definitions/term"
      }
    }
  },
  "definitions": {
    "category": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "title"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
          "description": "Stable category slug referenced by terms, using the taxonomy segment grammar. The display title can change without changing references.",
          "maxLength": 60
        },
        "title": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Required display heading in the product's language, distinct from the stable category ID.",
          "maxLength": 120
        },
        "purpose": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Optional description of which terms belong in the category.",
          "maxLength": 300
        }
      }
    },
    "term": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "term",
        "definition"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "term": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Exact word or phrase used in record prose. Matching is case-sensitive and whole-word: Consignee and consignee are distinct, and neither matches inside a longer word. Duplicate term definitions are linter errors.",
          "maxLength": 120
        },
        "category": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
          "description": "Optional reference to one declared category ID. An undeclared ID is a linter error. Absence leaves the term uncategorised and does not create an implicit Other category or assert that classification is complete.",
          "maxLength": 60
        },
        "definition": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Meaning of the term in the product's language, including distinctions from related terms. Behavioural promises belong in record contracts rather than in this naming authority.",
          "maxLength": 1500
        },
        "renderings": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Per-locale wording for the term, keyed by locale. Core currently does not interpret or validate these values beyond this schema.",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "patternProperties": {
            "^[a-z]{2,3}(-[A-Za-z0-9]{2,8})*$": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/plugin-manifest.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/plugin-manifest.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET plugin manifest (plugin.json)",
  "description": "What a plugin declares about itself: who it is, which host API it needs, where its module is, which surfaces it claims, which tools it asks for and which binary it brings.\n\nA manifest asks; it grants nothing. Every tool, variable and agent tool named here is refused until the host's grants.json for this plugin answers it. The id is taken from the directory the host installed the plugin into, never from this file alone — a manifest that could name itself could claim another plugin's grants.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "id",
    "name",
    "version",
    "api",
    "entry"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-z0-9-]{1,64}$",
      "description": "The name the host knows this plugin by. Lowercase letters, digits and '-' only, at most 64 characters. It may not be the id of a plugin the host already ships."
    },
    "name": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "maxLength": 80,
      "description": "The name shown in the plugin management."
    },
    "version": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?$",
      "description": "The plugin's own version, semver. Independent of the host's."
    },
    "api": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0,
      "description": "The host API this plugin needs. A host that does not offer it does not load the plugin and says which number it offers instead. 0 means the interface is not stable yet and may break."
    },
    "entry": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^(?!/)(?!.*\\.\\.)[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.m?js$",
      "description": "Path of the ES module inside the package, relative, built JavaScript (.js or .mjs). The module's default export receives the host object. A package arrives built."
    },
    "description": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 500
    },
    "author": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 200
    },
    "license": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 100,
      "description": "An SPDX identifier, e.g. MIT."
    },
    "homepage": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^https://",
      "maxLength": 500
    },
    "areas": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9-]{1,64}$"
      },
      "uniqueItems": true,
      "description": "The whole surfaces this plugin claims from the host (areas.register). A second plugin claiming the same name is refused at load."
    },
    "slots": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "enum": [
          "surface.section",
          "record.panel",
          "scenario.panel",
          "header.action"
        ]
      },
      "uniqueItems": true,
      "description": "The slots this plugin mounts into."
    },
    "tools": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*\\.[a-z][a-z0-9.-]*$"
      },
      "uniqueItems": true,
      "description": "Every tool this plugin will call through the host bus (bus.call) — host tools such as repo.write, and the tools of its own sidecar. Declared is not granted. The reserved name facet.lint is a tool of the plugin's own sidecar that 'facet lint' calls with the registry's records and the files reads allows, and that answers with findings; like any tool it must be granted."
    },
    "ai_tools": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "The subset of tools offered to the agent. Each must also appear in tools, and is granted separately from it.",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "tool",
          "description",
          "input"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "tool": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 1000
          },
          "input": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "A JSON Schema object, passed to the model as written."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "events": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "listens": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "uniqueItems": true
        },
        "emits": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "uniqueItems": true,
          "description": "Every event name must start with this plugin's id and a dot; the bus refuses anything else."
        }
      }
    },
    "reads": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "oneOf": [
          {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*(/[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)*$"
          },
          {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "dir",
              "ext"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "dir": {
                "type": "string",
                "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*(/[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)*$"
              },
              "ext": {
                "type": "array",
                "minItems": 1,
                "uniqueItems": true,
                "items": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^\\.[a-z0-9]{1,10}$",
                  "not": {
                    "enum": [
                      ".env",
                      ".pem",
                      ".key",
                      ".p12",
                      ".pfx",
                      ".kdbx",
                      ".htpasswd"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "uniqueItems": true,
      "description": "Directories, relative to the registry root, this plugin may read through the repo.list and repo.read host tools. A plain string reads .md files only. The object form {\"dir\", \"ext\"} names the extensions readable in that directory (for example [\".dmn\"]); each is lowercase, one dot, at most ten characters, and extensions that conventionally hold secrets (.env, .pem, .key, .p12, .pfx, .kdbx, .htpasswd) are refused. A directory absent from here, or a file whose extension the entry does not list, is refused the same way an undeclared tool is. No segment may start with a dot, so \".\", \"..\" and hidden directories are refused; the host checks the same grammar again at every call (facet.ValidReadDir, facet.ValidReadExt) and refuses a directory that resolves outside the repository."
    },
    "sidecar": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "bin",
        "sha256"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A binary this plugin brings. In a package it lies at the root as <bin>-<os>-<arch>, with .exe for windows.",
      "properties": {
        "bin": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}$",
          "description": "The base name. The host appends the platform; never a path."
        },
        "env": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*$"
          },
          "uniqueItems": true,
          "description": "Names of environment variables, never values. The sidecar sees only the intersection of this list and what grants.json allows."
        },
        "ai_env": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*$"
          },
          "uniqueItems": true,
          "description": "The subset of env the sidecar may see when the agent is the caller. Each must also appear in env, and is granted separately under grants.json ai_env; a sidecar started for an agent call sees only the intersection of env, ai_env, grants.env and grants.ai_env. Absent means the agent's sidecar gets no variable."
        },
        "sha256": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Checksum per '<os>-<arch>', written by 'facet plugin pack' from the actual file. A package ships only the platforms it has; an empty map is allowed only for a plugin without a package (one shipped with the host, whose sums the host's build measures).",
          "propertyNames": {
            "pattern": "^(linux|darwin|windows)-(amd64|arm64)$"
          },
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/policy.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/policy.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET Policy Record",
  "description": "Schema for a FACET policy record (FACET specification, Appendix A.2).",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "id",
    "intent",
    "contract",
    "lineage"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "const": "0.1",
      "description": "FACET schema version. Must be '0.1'."
    },
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^policy/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$",
      "description": "Canonical policy ID in the form policy/<domain>/<name> (lowercase kebab-case)."
    },
    "intent": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "summary"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "summary": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Human-readable description of what this policy mandates and why."
        },
        "regulatory_basis": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Optional reference to the regulation, standard, or internal directive that mandates this policy (e.g. 'GDPR Art. 17', 'SOC 2 CC6.1')."
        },
        "decision_records": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "References to ADR or other decision records that motivated this policy.",
          "default": []
        }
      }
    },
    "contract": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "clauses"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "clauses": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/clause"
          },
          "description": "Normative clauses that constitute this policy. Each clause has a stable ID and a requirement statement."
        }
      }
    },
    "scope": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "governs_features": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Feature IDs (domain/capability/feature) that this policy governs.",
          "default": []
        },
        "governs_domains": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Domain names (e.g. 'billing', 'catalog') that this policy applies to in their entirety.",
          "default": []
        }
      }
    },
    "verification": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "compliance_checks": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/compliance_check"
          },
          "description": "Automated or manual checks that verify compliance with this policy.",
          "default": []
        },
        "audit_artifacts": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Paths or URLs to audit reports, evidence logs, or certification documents.",
          "default": []
        }
      }
    },
    "lineage": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "owner",
        "created_at"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "owner": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/owner"
        },
        "created_at": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "ISO 8601 date when this record was first created."
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "definitions": {
    "clause": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "requirement"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Stable identifier for this clause (e.g. 'clause-1', 'ret-30d')."
        },
        "requirement": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The normative requirement text for this clause (MUST/SHALL/SHOULD language preferred)."
        }
      }
    },
    "compliance_check": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "cadence"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Stable identifier for this compliance check."
        },
        "cadence": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "How often the check is performed (e.g. 'daily', 'quarterly', 'on-deploy')."
        }
      }
    },
    "owner": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "team"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "team": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Owning team name (matches Conventional Commits scope)."
        },
        "individual": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Optional email of the individual DRI for this policy."
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/spec-lock.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/spec-lock.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET specification lock",
  "type": "object",
  "propertyNames": {
    "type": "string",
    "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
  },
  "additionalProperties": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
      "repo",
      "follow",
      "format",
      "files",
      "scenarios"
    ],
    "properties": {
      "repo": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1
      },
      "follow": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1
      },
      "format": {
        "enum": [
          "facet-spec",
          "gherkin",
          "openspec",
          "speckit",
          "gherkin-markdown",
          "kiro",
          "bmad",
          "gauge"
        ]
      },
      "commit": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^([0-9a-f]{40}|[0-9a-f]{64})$"
      },
      "files": {
        "type": "object",
        "propertyNames": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^([0-9]{3}-|[0-9]+-[0-9]+-)?[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(/([0-9]{3}-|[0-9]+-[0-9]+-)?[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)*$"
        },
        "additionalProperties": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "status",
            "language"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "status": {
              "enum": [
                "draft",
                "approved",
                "deprecated"
              ]
            },
            "language": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "scenarios": {
        "type": "object",
        "propertyNames": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^([0-9]{3}-|[0-9]+-[0-9]+-)?[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(/([0-9]{3}-|[0-9]+-[0-9]+-)?[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)*#[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
        },
        "additionalProperties": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "commit",
            "steps"
          ],
          "if": {
            "required": [
              "binding"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "binding": {
                "const": "provenance"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "required": [
              "text"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "sequence": false,
              "context": false
            }
          },
          "else": {
            "required": [
              "context",
              "sequence"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "text": false
            }
          },
          "properties": {
            "commit": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^([0-9a-f]{40}|[0-9a-f]{64})$"
            },
            "steps": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$"
            },
            "context": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$"
            },
            "binding": {
              "enum": [
                "exact",
                "provenance"
              ]
            },
            "text": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "sequence": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": [
                "steps"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "steps": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "required": [
                      "type",
                      "text"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "type": {
                        "enum": [
                          "Unknown",
                          "Context",
                          "Action",
                          "Outcome"
                        ]
                      },
                      "text": {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      "doc_string": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "additionalProperties": false,
                        "required": [
                          "media_type",
                          "content"
                        ],
                        "properties": {
                          "media_type": {
                            "type": "string"
                          },
                          "content": {
                            "type": "string"
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "data_table": {
                        "type": "array",
                        "items": {
                          "type": "array",
                          "items": {
                            "type": "string"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                },
                "examples": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "string"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/spec.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/spec.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET spec frontmatter",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema",
    "id",
    "title",
    "status",
    "owner"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema": {
      "const": "facet-spec/0.1"
    },
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)*$"
    },
    "title": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
    },
    "status": {
      "enum": [
        "draft",
        "approved",
        "deprecated"
      ]
    },
    "owner": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
    },
    "language": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "default": "en"
    },
    "case_tag": {
      "enum": [
        "case",
        "id"
      ],
      "default": "case"
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/taxonomy.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/taxonomy.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET Product Taxonomy",
  "description": "Declares product domains and capabilities used by feature ids (FACET §4.4). Records supply the third id segment. Optional: without a taxonomy, no taxonomy checks run. This naming authority carries no contract, anchor or lifecycle.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "domains"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "0.1"
      ],
      "description": "FACET schema family this taxonomy was written under."
    },
    "domains": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Product domains, keyed by the segment records use as the first part of their id. A product domain, not a team and not a service: teams reorganise and ids are immutable, so an id built from an org chart is wrong on a schedule. The organisational axis already exists as lineage.owner.team on each record, and the two are deliberately separate.",
      "minProperties": 1,
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "patternProperties": {
        "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/domain"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "definitions": {
    "domain": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "title",
        "capabilities"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "title": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "What this domain is called in the product's own language — the name a user or an operator would use, not the directory it happens to live in."
        },
        "purpose": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Optional description of the domain's purpose, used to choose where a feature belongs."
        },
        "classification": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/classification"
        },
        "owner": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "The team answering for this domain by default. It informs a record's lineage.owner and never replaces it: a record's owner is a claim about that feature, and a domain-level default that silently became one would be a claim nobody made.",
          "required": [
            "team"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "team": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "Team identifier, in whatever form the project's CODEOWNERS uses."
            }
          }
        },
        "capabilities": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Capabilities under this domain, keyed by the segment records use as the second part of their id. A capability is a stable noun group: the level at which a product's areas are named in a roadmap, above a single feature and below a whole domain.",
          "minProperties": 1,
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "patternProperties": {
            "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$": {
              "$ref": "#/definitions/capability"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "capability": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "One product capability. Its features are defined by records, avoiding a duplicate feature list that could disagree with them.",
      "required": [
        "title"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "title": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "What this capability is called in the product's own language."
        },
        "purpose": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Optional description of the capability's scope and boundaries."
        },
        "classification": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/classification"
        }
      }
    },
    "classification": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "core",
        "supporting",
        "generic"
      ],
      "description": "Strategic weight using Evans' subdomains: core differentiates the product; supporting is business-specific without differentiating it; generic is a solved problem that may be bought. Weight is independent of taxonomy depth, which is derived from ids. Classification belongs to domains or capabilities. An absent value means undecided; a capability without a value inherits its domain's classification."
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/schema/variants.schema.json --
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/facet-framework/core/main/schema/variants.schema.json",
  "title": "FACET Variant Map",
  "description": "Declares a deployment's variants and the paths belonging to each. A variant is an independently deployable place where a feature can exist or not exist: clients, but also backends, workers and pipelines whenever 'does this feature exist there yet?' has its own answer. A rewrite duplicates all of those, so restricting variants to clients would classify legacy/api and v2/api as shared code — which is doubly wrong, since they are competing rather than shared, and it would make 'the backend is migrated, the web client is not' inexpressible. Genuinely shared libraries and infrastructure go under 'shared'; they are anchored like any other code but prove no variant.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "variants"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "0.1"
      ],
      "description": "FACET schema family this map was written under."
    },
    "variants": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Surfaces, keyed by the name records use in their 'variants' block.",
      "minProperties": 1,
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "patternProperties": {
        "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "paths"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "paths": {
              "$ref": "#/definitions/paths"
            },
            "description": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "What this variant is, for a reader who does not already know."
            },
            "replaces": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Another declared variant that this one is replacing. How a rewrite is modelled: v2-api replaces legacy-api, both exist while the migration runs, and per-variant lifecycle shows how far it has got. Used for reporting — grouping by migration, counting what remains, listing what blocks retiring the old variant. It drives no lint on purpose: a check firing on every unmigrated feature would warn once per record for the duration of the migration."
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "shared": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Code belonging to no single variant: shared libraries and infrastructure serving several of them without being one. Anchors here resolve for navigation and drift detection but satisfy no variant's presence requirement. Two competing implementations of the same thing — legacy and its rewrite — are not shared; they are separate variants.",
      "required": [
        "paths"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "paths": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/paths"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "definitions": {
    "paths": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "description": "Glob patterns, relative to the repository root. Patterns may match files as well as directories, because the most common multi-variant layout there is — React Native's platform extensions — puts Button.ios.tsx and Button.web.tsx in the same directory, which a directory-only map cannot express.\n\nWhen several patterns match one file, the longest matching pattern wins, as in routing. Without that rule the order of entries decides the outcome and two readers of the same file reach different conclusions.\n\nA file matched by more than one variant at the same specificity is shared, by the same reasoning as an explicit 'shared' entry: exclusivity is the test for presence.",
      "items": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1
      }
    }
  }
}
-- docs/facets/framework/FACET.md --
# The FACET Framework 0.1.0

**Feature-Anchored Canonical Executable Truth**
_A specification for product-feature documentation as single source of truth, designed for the age of AI-assisted development._

**Status:** Reference specification
**Version:** 0.1.0
**License:** Apache-2.0

> **Implementation scope (informative).** This document defines framework requirements; the source release does not claim complete implementation of every reference interface or projection. Its bundled MCP server exposes five of the twelve reference tool names in §6.2: `feature_find`, `feature_get`, `anchor_resolve`, `anchor_list` and `registry_validate`. The other seven reference tool names and the optional feature-proposal interfaces in §6.4 are not supplied under those names. Additional tools do not establish full conformance. This repository provides the registry engine and CLI, together with agent skill bundles and the plugin and marketplace files that install them into Claude Code and Codex. The local reader is not included; it belongs to Atlas, a separate product that is not included in this release. Generator integrations described here are deployment responsibilities, not a claim that this release supplies every pipeline.

